; A merged atomname2type.n2t generated by n2t_atom() for different MINFF atomtypes
; Note that this file might not work right away for your structure
; Comment or uncomment the different lines to fit your needs..
; Columns: Element  AtomType  Charge  Mass[u]  CN  [NeighborElement  Distance(nm)]
;
; Covers most if not all MINFF atomtypes. The edge and substitution-site entries (He, Ale,
; Mge, Fee2, Fee3, Oal, Osi, Oalh, Oalsi, Oalhh, Oahs, Odsub) follow the MINFF
; typing rules; their bond distances are representative values for the element
; pair. Distances only control bond detection in x2top (a +-10% window); the
; atomtype itself is chosen by element name and coordination number alone.
;
; The charges listed for the O atomtypes are per-environment examples. The
; oxygen charge in MINFF is not a fixed property of the atomtype: it is computed
; for each site from the charge-smearing equation of Lammers et al. 2017
; (doi:10.1016/j.jcis.2016.11.084), which is how the atom and atomipy libraries
; handle isomorphic substitution and edge sites. The patched x2top can do the
; same with the -smear flag, in which case the charge column below is only a
; fallback for the O atomtypes.
;
; IMPORTANT: where two entries share the same element, coordination number and
; neighbour elements, x2top takes the FIRST one and the rest are unreachable.
; In this merged file that affects: He (shadowed by H), Feo3 (shadowed by Feo2), Fet3 
; (shadowed by Fet2), Fee2 (by Fee3), Mgo (by Mgh), and several Ob/Obt/Oh/Op variants. 
; For a specific mineral, comment out the entries that do not apply, or pass a
; mineral-specific file with "gmx x2top -n2t mymineral.n2t".
;
